tion:** [`ops/sandbox/xoras_os_ram_sandbox.sh#L17`](file:///Volumes/Untitled/SSOT_Agentic_Brain_v1.1.0_ENGINEERING_RELEASE/ops/sandbox/xoras_os_ram_sandbox.sh#L17)\n* **Evidence:** `AUDIT_LOG=\"/User\n<truncated 6781 bytes>\nxoras_sandbox.py`)**:\n   - Implement `os.path.realpath()` for all path arguments to resolve symlinks and relative traversal (`../`).\n   - Dynamically compute `workspace_dir` using `os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"../../../..\"))`.\n   - Restrict process execution by default; maintain an explicit allowlist of safe binaries rather than blocking a fixed list of file tools.\n   - Refactor shell string splitting to parse full POSIX shell syntax via `shlex.split`.\n\n3. **E2E & Consensus Optimization (`xoras_vector_db.py`, `xoras_shm_bft.py`)**:\n   - Fix `migrate_json_data()` path resolution in `xoras_vector_db.py` to always check `base_dir/Source/XORAS_ACTIVE_KNOWLEDGE.json`.\n   - Dynamic `shm_name` generation using `f\"xoras_shm_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}\"`.\n   - Optimize BFT spin-backoff loop in `xoras_shm_bft.py` to achieve guaranteed `< 0.8ms` latency across multi-process iterations.\n\n---\n\n## Remaining Questions & Gaps\n1. **macOS `sandbox-exec` Deprecation Path:** macOS Apple Silicon builds recommend SBPL (Sandbox Policy Language) compiled profiles via `sandbox_init` or Docker Desktop runtime. Host environment integration testing for hardware container isolation remains unverified without active Docker daemon bindings.\n2. **Shared Memory Access Control on Multi-User macOS:** POSIX shared memory segments created via Python `multiprocessing.shared_memory` inherit user umask; further research is required to enforce kernel ACLs on shared memory buffers across sovereign worker boundaries.\n3. **Follow-up Focus:** The next iteration should prioritize enforcing `realpath` canonicalization in `xoras_sandbox.py`, fixing `xoras_vector_db.py` path resolution to unblock the 11 failing unit tests, and establishing a dynamic UUID-based shared memory allocation for `xoras_shm_bft.py`.\n\nThoroughly review the findings above. Carefully check if they fully address every single aspect of the user's question — do not skip any part. Iterate if necessary following the **Workflow** in your system prompt.\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>","truncated_fields":["content"]}
